Extended in _document rather than by moving the last word's end like _shorten_stretched does: the words' timing is what was heard, and only the display needs to last longer. Merging into a neighbour (_merge_short) was not widened instead: these words are separated by pauses longer than merge_gap, often from another line of dialogue, so joining them would show two lines as one. Capped at the next subtitle's start so subtitles never overlap; when the next one starts within 1 s, the short one stays short (3 of 411 in the 2 h Japanese film).
